foundation.question_text:
The dot plot shows the number of days taken for bean seeds to sprout. What is the range?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large},scale=0.8]
\draw[->] (-0.5,0)--(8.8,0); \foreach \x in {0,...,8} {\draw (\x,0.08)--(\x,-0.08); \node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\x,0) {$\x$};}
\foreach \x/\c in {2/1,3/2,4/4,5/2,7/1} {\foreach \k in {1,...,\c} {\fill (\x,{0.34*\k}) circle (2.2pt);}}
\node[below] at (5,-0.9) {Days to sprout};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The dot plot shows leaves counted on seedlings. What is the mode?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large},scale=0.8]
\draw[->] (-0.5,0)--(8.8,0); \foreach \x in {0,...,8} {\draw (\x,0.08)--(\x,-0.08); \node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\x,0) {$\x$};}
\foreach \x/\c in {2/1,3/3,4/2,5/5,6/2,8/1} {\foreach \k in {1,...,\c} {\fill (\x,{0.34*\k}) circle (2.2pt);}}
\node[below] at (5,-0.9) {Number of leaves};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The dot plot shows seed-pod lengths in centimetres. Does this dataset have a mode?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large},scale=0.8]
\draw[->] (-0.5,0)--(7.8,0); \foreach \x in {0,...,7} {\draw (\x,0.08)--(\x,-0.08); \node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\x,0) {$\x$};}
\foreach \x in {1,2,3,4,5,6,7} {\fill (\x,0.34) circle (2.2pt);}
\node[below] at (4,-0.9) {Pod length (cm)};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The dot plot shows flowers on young plants. What are the modes?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large},scale=0.8]
\draw[->] (-0.5,0)--(6.8,0); \foreach \x in {0,...,6} {\draw (\x,0.08)--(\x,-0.08); \node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\x,0) {$\x$};}
\foreach \x/\c in {0/1,1/2,2/4,3/2,4/1,5/4,6/1} {\foreach \k in {1,...,\c} {\fill (\x,{0.34*\k}) circle (2.2pt);}}
\node[below] at (3,-0.9) {Number of flowers};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The paired dot plots show plant heights in two trays. Which tray has the greater range?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large},scale=0.78]
\draw[->] (-0.5,0)--(8.8,0); \draw[->] (-0.5,2.3)--(8.8,2.3); \foreach \x in {0,...,8} {\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\x,0) {$\x$}; \node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\x,2.3) {$\x$};}
\foreach \x/\c in {2/1,3/2,4/3,5/2,6/1} {\foreach \k in {1,...,\c} {\fill (\x,{0.32*\k}) circle (2.2pt);}}
\foreach \x/\c in {1/1,3/2,4/2,7/2,8/1} {\foreach \k in {1,...,\c} {\fill (\x,{2.3+0.32*\k}) circle (2.2pt);}}
\node[left] at (-0.55,0.8) {Tray A}; \node[left] at (-0.55,3.1) {Tray B}; \node[below] at (4.5,-0.9) {Height (cm)};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The paired dot plots show shoots on plants in two plots. Compare their modes.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large},scale=0.78]
\draw[->] (-0.5,0)--(7.8,0); \draw[->] (-0.5,2.3)--(7.8,2.3); \foreach \x in {0,...,7} {\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\x,0) {$\x$}; \node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\x,2.3) {$\x$};}
\foreach \x/\c in {1/1,2/2,3/4,4/2,6/1} {\foreach \k in {1,...,\c} {\fill (\x,{0.32*\k}) circle (2.2pt);}}
\foreach \x/\c in {2/1,4/2,5/4,6/2,7/1} {\foreach \k in {1,...,\c} {\fill (\x,{2.3+0.32*\k}) circle (2.2pt);}}
\node[left] at (-0.55,0.8) {Plot P}; \node[left] at (-0.55,3.1) {Plot Q}; \node[below] at (4,-0.9) {Number of shoots};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

development.question_text:
The paired dot plots show germination times. Both have mode $4$. Which bed has the greater range, and by how much?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large},scale=0.78]
\draw[->] (-0.5,0)--(8.8,0); \draw[->] (-0.5,2.3)--(8.8,2.3); \foreach \x in {0,...,8} {\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\x,0) {$\x$}; \node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\x,2.3) {$\x$};}
\foreach \x/\c in {2/1,3/2,4/5,5/2,6/1} {\foreach \k in {1,...,\c} {\fill (\x,{0.32*\k}) circle (2.2pt);}}
\foreach \x/\c in {1/1,3/2,4/4,6/2,8/1} {\foreach \k in {1,...,\c} {\fill (\x,{2.3+0.32*\k}) circle (2.2pt);}}
\node[left] at (-0.55,0.8) {Bed A}; \node[left] at (-0.55,3.1) {Bed B}; \node[below] at (4.5,-0.9) {Days};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Two seedling datasets have the same range. What feature is different in the displays?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large},scale=0.78]
\draw[->] (-0.5,0)--(7.8,0); \draw[->] (-0.5,2.3)--(7.8,2.3); \foreach \x in {0,...,7} {\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\x,0) {$\x$}; \node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\x,2.3) {$\x$};}
\foreach \x/\c in {1/1,2/2,3/4,4/2,7/1} {\foreach \k in {1,...,\c} {\fill (\x,{0.32*\k}) circle (2.2pt);}}
\foreach \x/\c in {1/1,3/2,5/4,6/2,7/1} {\foreach \k in {1,...,\c} {\fill (\x,{2.3+0.32*\k}) circle (2.2pt);}}
\node[left] at (-0.55,0.8) {Set C}; \node[left] at (-0.55,3.1) {Set D}; \node[below] at (4,-0.9) {Stem length (cm)};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Which compost trial has results that are more spread out? Use the range.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large},scale=0.78]
\draw[->] (-0.5,0)--(8.8,0); \draw[->] (-0.5,2.3)--(8.8,2.3); \foreach \x in {0,...,8} {\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\x,0) {$\x$}; \node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\x,2.3) {$\x$};}
\foreach \x/\c in {2/1,3/3,4/4,5/2} {\foreach \k in {1,...,\c} {\fill (\x,{0.32*\k}) circle (2.2pt);}}
\foreach \x/\c in {0/1,2/2,4/3,6/2,8/1} {\foreach \k in {1,...,\c} {\fill (\x,{2.3+0.32*\k}) circle (2.2pt);}}
\node[left] at (-0.55,0.8) {Trial X}; \node[left] at (-0.55,3.1) {Trial Y}; \node[below] at (4,-0.9) {New leaves};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A gardener says the two displays have the same typical result because both modes are $4$. Is the claim supported?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large},scale=0.78]
\draw[->] (-0.5,0)--(8.8,0); \draw[->] (-0.5,2.3)--(8.8,2.3); \foreach \x in {0,...,8} {\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\x,0) {$\x$}; \node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\x,2.3) {$\x$};}
\foreach \x/\c in {2/1,3/2,4/5,5/1,6/1} {\foreach \k in {1,...,\c} {\fill (\x,{0.32*\k}) circle (2.2pt);}}
\foreach \x/\c in {1/1,2/1,4/4,7/2,8/1} {\foreach \k in {1,...,\c} {\fill (\x,{2.3+0.32*\k}) circle (2.2pt);}}
\node[left] at (-0.55,0.8) {Tray M}; \node[left] at (-0.55,3.1) {Tray N}; \node[below] at (4.5,-0.9) {Growth (cm)};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
